---

<DocsLayout
  title="huberclaude quickstart — first session in 5 minutes"
  description="Run your first huberclaude session: start the agent in a repo, sign in to OpenRouter, give it a task, and review the diff."
  heading="quickstart"
  lede="From a fresh install to a reviewed diff in about five minutes."
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="start">1. start the agent</h2>
  <p>Run it inside any repository (or an empty directory):</p>
  <pre><code>cd your-repo
huberclaude</code></pre>
  <p>If you haven't <a href="/docs/installation/">installed it</a> yet, build it from source first.</p>

  <h2 id="login">2. sign in to openrouter</h2>
  <p>
    Type <code>/login</code> and paste your
    <a href="https://openrouter.ai/keys" rel="noopener">OpenRouter API key</a>. Then type
    <code>/model</code> to pick a model (the default is <code>qwen/qwen3-coder</code>).
    No other provider setup is needed. See the <a href="/docs/providers/">OpenRouter page</a>
    for details and env-var setup.
  </p>

  <h2 id="first-task">3. give it a task</h2>
  <p>Write a task the way you'd brief a teammate:</p>
  <pre><code>&gt; add retry with exponential backoff to the fetch client, then run the tests</code></pre>
  <p>
    The agent streams its plan, tool calls, and edits live as it reads files, searches,
    edits, and runs commands. Tool use is permission-gated: you approve the first use of
    anything sensitive and can manage rules later with <code>/permissions</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="review">5. review the changes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>/diff</code>: view uncommitted changes and per-turn diffs.</li>
    <li><code>/rewind</code>: restore code and/or conversation to a previous point.</li>
    <li><code>/usage</code>: check your OpenRouter balance and spend.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Nothing is committed unless you ask for it, and every change stays reviewable.</p>

  <h2 id="next-steps">next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Browse the <a href="/docs/slash-commands/">slash command reference</a> for sessions, context, review, and more.</li>
    <li>Script it with <code>huberclaude -p "explain this repo"</code>. See the <a href="/docs/cli-reference/">CLI reference</a>.</li>
    <li>Make it yours with <a href="/docs/configuration/">configuration</a> and <a href="/docs/keybindings/">keybindings</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
